== Prep the Tofu ==

Drain @tofu{15%oz}(super or extra-firm) and press gently with paper towels to remove excess liquid. Place in an airtight container and freeze overnight or at least ~{8%hours}.

When ready to cook, defrost the tofu on low heat in the #microwave{}, stopping every few minutes to press excess liquid from the tofu with paper towels. Break the tofu block into 1-2" pieces or chunks. Set aside.

== Prep the Wet & Dry ==

In a large shallow bowl, mix together @soy milk{1¼%cup} and @apple cider vinegar{1½%tbsp}.

In a separate large shallow bowl, mix together @all-purpose flour{1%cup}(about 160g), @corn starch{¼%cup}(about 30g), @yellow cornmeal{¼%cup}(about 45g), @bread crumbs{¼%cup}(about 25g), @nutritional yeast{1%tbsp}, @dried onion flakes{1%tbsp}, @garlic powder{1%tsp}, @smoked paprika{1%tsp}, @black pepper{¼%tsp}, and @sea salt{½%tsp} until evenly distributed.

== Make the Tofu ==

Preheat #air fryer{} to 400°F.

Dip your tofu chunks into the soy milk mixture and let soak for ~{1%minute}. Then place them in the dry mixture and pat the breading into the tofu.

Place the tofu back into the wet mixture (just enough to make it wet again — don't soak), then dip into the dry mixture a second time. (wet → dry → wet → dry).

Place the tofu onto a parchment-lined air fryer basket. Brush with @neutral oil{1%tbsp} and spray all sides with @cooking spray{}.

Air fry at 400°F for ~{10%minutes}. Flip the tofu and reapply cooking spray and oil. Cook for a further ~{6%minutes}. Serve warm.
